	"_comment": [
		"3.1.2 instance native after 'Save' in the old admin UI with all nine messengers and three devices.",
		"Derived from 3.1.2 admin/lib/index_m.js save(): every table key from data.js keysCntrlInput is stored as { ids: <table rows>, finalIds: <createArray()> }; finalIds is dropped when empty (devices, default, custom, status).",
		"Row ids come from createId(): numbers for rows from io-package defaults, strings ('0', '1', ...) for rows added in the UI.",
		"linkedDevice.finalIds joins the 'devices' row (type, consumption -> pathConsumption, switch -> pathSwitch, startText, endText) with the dynamic linkedDevice row (enabled, name, messenger id lists from multi-selects as string arrays, timer as input string, autoOff, abort, id).",
		"Messenger finalIds are written by createArray() but 3.1.2 main.js reads the raw rows native.<messenger>.ids (createObjMessenger -> getDataFromAdmin keeps only entries with an id).",
		"Pushover row columns: name, inst, title, deviceID, prio (normal/high/quiet/confirmation), sound (options carry a leading space in data.js), ttl. Telegram: name, inst, key (username/firstname/chatID), username.",
		"Status texts: status.ids[0] { stateAction, stateStandby, stateOff } ('device off' is the admin default for stateOff).",
		"Device 'Trockner' carries an unknown field 'gotify' (commented column in data.js) to exercise the warning."
